    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/d217efea-b0cc-452b-b30e-217aacb10a94.png\" style=\"width:1.96042in;height:1.64653in\" /><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is a focal chord and&nbsp;<math><mi>S</mi></math> is the focus<br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp; (<math><mi>R</mi></math> is the foot of the perpendicular from&nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi></math> on <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Length of <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is equal to the length of latus rectum<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>2.5</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6.2</mn><mn>5</mn></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></math>",
